Legal reference: The Right of Children to Free and Compulsory Education Act,2009,Section no 28
Category: Educational
Description: The appropriate Government and the local authority shall ensure that the following norms and standards are specified in respect of a school, namely: (a) infrastructure including school building, teaching staff and learning equipment;

Legal reference: National Council for Teacher Education Act,1993,Section no 12
Category: Educational
Description: (1) The Council shall perform, inter alia, the following functions, namely:— (a) to achieve planned and coordinated development of the teacher education system throughout the country;

Legal reference: Indian Institutes of Technology Act,1961,Section no 6
Category: Educational
Description: (1) Subject to the provisions of this Act, the Institutes shall exercise the following powers and perform the following functions, namely:— (a) to provide for instruction and research in such branches of engineering and technology, sciences and arts as the Institutes may think fit and for the advancement of learning and dissemination of knowledge in such branches;

Legal reference: Indian Institutes of Technology Act,1961,Section no 27
Category: Educational
Description: (1) The Institutes may, subject to the approval of the Visitor, make rules consistent with this Act and the Statutes to regulate— (a) the formation of departments and the assignment of subjects to such departments;

Legal reference: Indian Institutes of Technology Act,1961,Section no 3
Category: Educational
Description: (1) The following institutions, to wit:- (a) the Indian Institute of Technology, Kharagpur, in the State of West Bengal;

Legal reference: Indian Institutes of Technology Act,1961,Section no 10
Category: Educational
Description: (1) There shall be a Senate of the Institute which shall consist of the following persons, namely:- (a) the Director;

Legal reference: Indian Institutes of Technology Act,1961,Section no 11
Category: Educational
Description: (1) The Senate shall have the following powers and functions, namely:- (a) to prescribe the courses of study and the syllabi for the examinations to be held for degrees, diplomas and other academic distinctions;

Legal reference: Indian Institutes of Technology Act,1961,Section no 13
Category: Educational
Description: (1) There shall be a Finance Committee of the Institute which shall consist of the following members, namely:- (a) the Director;

Legal reference: Indian Institutes of Technology Act,1961,Section no 15
Category: Educational
Description: (1) There shall be a Building and Works Committee of the Institute which shall consist of the following members, namely:- (a) the Director;

Legal reference: Indian Institutes of Technology Act,1961,Section no 17
Category: Educational
Description: The following shall be the authorities of the Institute, namely:- (a) the Board of Governors;

Legal reference: Indian Institutes of Technology Act,1961,Section no 19
Category: Educational
Description: (1) Subject to the provisions of this Act, the Statutes may provide for all or any of the following matters, namely:- (a) the conferment of honorary degrees;

Legal reference: Indian Institutes of Technology Act,1961,Section no 23
Category: Educational
Description: (1) Subject to the provisions of this Act and the Statutes, the Ordinances may provide for all or any of the following matters, namely:- (a) the admission of students to the Institutes;

Legal reference: The National Institutes of Technology Act, 2007,Section 9
Category: Educational
Description: (1) There shall be a Board of Governors for every Institute, consisting of the following members, namely:- (a) the Chairperson to be nominated by the Visitor;

Legal reference: The National Institutes of Technology Act, 2007,Section 10
Category: Educational
Description: (1) Subject to the provisions of this Act, the Board of every Institute shall have the power to make Statutes consistent with this Act and the rules made thereunder, to provide for all or any of the following matters, namely:- (a) the formation of departments of teaching;

Legal reference: Hindu Marriage Act,1955,Section no 5
Category: Family
Description: A marriage may be solemnized between any two Hindus, if the following conditions are fulfilled, namely: (i) neither party has a spouse living at the time of the marriage;

Legal reference: Hindu Marriage Act,1955,Section no 13
Category: Family
Description: Any marriage solemnized, whether before or after the commencement of this Act, may, on a petition presented by either the husband or the wife, be dissolved by a decree of divorce on the ground that the other party: (i) has, after the solemnization of the marriage, had voluntary sexual intercourse with any person other than his or her spouse;

Legal reference: Hindu Marriage Act,1955,Section no 26
Category: Family
Description: Save as otherwise expressly provided in this Act, (a) any text, rule or interpretation of Hindu law or any custom or usage as part of that law in force immediately before the commencement of this Act shall cease to have effect with respect to any matter for which provision is made in this Act;

Legal reference: Muslim Personal Law (Shariat) Application Act,1937,Section No 2
Category: Family
Description: Not withstanding any customs or usage to the contrary, in all questions (save questions relating to agricultural land) regarding intestate succession, special property of females, including personal property inherited or obtained under contract or gift or any other provision of Personal Law;

Legal reference: Special Marriage Act,1954,Section no 4
Category: Family
Description: Not withstanding anything contained in any other law for the time being in force relating to the solemnization of marriages, a marriage between any two persons may be solemnized under this Act, if at the time of the marriage the following conditions are fulfilled, namely: (a) neither party has a spouse living;

Legal reference: Protection of Women from Domestic Violence Act,2005,Section no 3
Category: Family
Description: (a) ""aggrieved person"" means any woman who is, or has been, in a domestic relationship with the respondent and who alleges to have been subjected to any act of domestic violence by the respondent;

Legal reference: Protection of Women from Domestic Violence Act,2005,Section no 5
Category: Family
Description: For the purposes of this Act, any act, omission or commission or conduct of the respondent shall constitute domestic violence in case it - (a) harms or injures or endangers the health, safety, life, limb or well-being, whether mental or physical, of the aggrieved person or tends to do so and includes causing physical abuse, sexual abuse, verbal and emotional abuse and economic abuse;

Legal reference: Hindu Adoption and Maintenance Act,1956,Section no 9
Category: Family
Description: No person shall be capable of being taken in adoption unless the following conditions are fulfilled, namely: (i) he or she is a Hindu;

Legal reference: Hindu Succession Act,1956,Section No 4
Category: Family
Description: (1) Save as otherwise expressly provided in this Act - (a) any text, rule or interpretation of Hindu law or any custom or usage as part of that law in force immediately before the commencement of this Act shall cease to have effect with respect to any matter for which provision is made in this Act;

Legal reference: Hindu Succession Act,1956,Section No 6
Category: Family
Description: (1) On and from the commencement of the Hindu Succession (Amendment) Act, 2005, in a Joint Hindu family governed by the Mitakshara law, the daughter of a coparcener shall - (a) by birth become a coparcener in her own right in the same manner as the son;

Legal reference: Indian Divorce Act,1869,Section No 17
Category: Family
Description: (1) The High Court may make rules consistent with this Act, - (a) for the guidance of officers in the issuing and registration of marriage licenses and certificates, and in the registration of divorces decreed by the High Court;

Legal reference: Guardians and Wards Act,1890,Section No 4
Category: Family
Description: In this Act, unless there is anything repugnant in the subject or context, - (a) ""minor"" means a person who, under the provisions of the Indian Majority Act, 1875 (9 of 1875);

Legal reference: Guardians and Wards Act,1890,Section No 5
Category: Family
Description: (1) If the Court is satisfied that it is for the welfare of a minor that an order should be made - (a) appointing a guardian of his person or property, or both; or (b) declaring a person to be such guardian;

Legal reference: Hindu Minority and Guardianship Act,1956,Section No 4
Category: Family
Description: Save as otherwise expressly provided in this Act, - (a) any text, rule or interpretation of Hindu law or any custom or usage as part of that law in force immediately before the commencement of this Act shall cease to have effect with respect to any matter for which provision is made in this Act;

Legal reference: Hindu Minority and Guardianship Act,1956,Section No 5
Category: Family
Description: The natural guardian of a Hindu minor, in respect of the minor's person as well as in respect of the minor's property (excluding his or her undivided interest in joint family property), are: (a) in the case of a boy or an unmarried girl - the father, and after him, the mother;

Legal reference: Muslim Women (Protection of Rights on Divorce) Act,1986,Section No 3
Category: Family
Description: Not withstanding anything contained in any other law for the time being in force, a divorced woman shall be entitled to - (a) a reasonable and fair provision and maintenance to be made and paid to her within the iddat period by her former husband;

Legal reference: Christian Marriage Act, 1872,Section 5
Category: Family
Description: (1) Marriages may be solemnized in India - (a) by any person who has received episcopal ordination, provided that the marriage be solemnized according to the rules, rites, ceremonies and customs of the Church of which he is a Minister;

Legal reference: Christian Marriage Act, 1872,Section 7
Category: Family
Description: (1) No marriage shall be valid if either of the parties thereto has a wife or husband living at the time of the marriage;

Legal reference: Parsi Marriage and Divorce Act, 1936,Section 3
Category: Family
Description: No marriage shall be valid if - (a) the contracting parties are related to each other in any of the degrees of consanguinity or affinity set forth in Schedule I;

Legal reference: Parsi Marriage and Divorce Act, 1936,Section 4
Category: Family
Description: A Parsi marriage shall not be valid unless - (a) it is solemnized according to the Parsi form of ceremony called 'Ashirvad' by a priest in the presence of two Parsi witnesses other than such priest;

Legal reference: Domestic Violence Act, 2005,Section 3
Category: Family
Description: For the purposes of this Act, any act, omission or commission or conduct of the respondent shall constitute domestic violence in case it - (a) harms or injures or endangers the health, safety, life, limb or well-being, whether mental or physical, of the aggrieved person or tends to do so and includes causing physical abuse, sexual abuse, verbal and emotional abuse and economic abuse;

Legal reference: Domestic Violence Act, 2005,Section 5
Category: Family
Description: A police officer, Protection Officer, service provider or Magistrate who has received a complaint of domestic violence or is otherwise present at the place of an incident of domestic violence or when the incident of domestic violence is reported to him, shall inform the aggrieved person - (a) of her right to make an application for obtaining a relief by way of a protection order, an order for monetary relief, a custody order, a residence order, a compensation order or more than one such order under this Act;

Legal reference: Domestic Violence Act, 2005,Section 18
Category: Family
Description: The Magistrate may, after giving the aggrieved person and the respondent an opportunity of being heard and on being prima facie satisfied that domestic violence has taken place or is likely to take place, pass a protection order in favour of the aggrieved person and prohibit the respondent from - (a) committing any act of domestic violence;

Legal reference: Domestic Violence Act, 2005,Section 19
Category: Family
Description: (1) While disposing of an application under sub-section (1) of section 12, the Magistrate may, on being satisfied that domestic violence has taken place, pass a residence order - (a) restraining the respondent from dispossessing or in any other manner disturbing the possession of the aggrieved person from the shared household;

Legal reference: Protection of Children from Sexual Offences (POCSO) Act, 2012,Section 2
Category: Family
Description: (1) In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires, - (d) 'child' means any person below the age of eighteen years;

Legal reference: Protection of Children from Sexual Offences (POCSO) Act, 2012,Section 3
Category: Family
Description: A person is said to commit 'penetrative sexual assault' if - (a) he penetrates his penis, to any extent, into the vagina, mouth, urethra or anus of a child or makes the child to do so with him or any other person;

Legal reference: Protection of Children from Sexual Offences (POCSO) Act, 2012,Section 5
Category: Family
Description: (1) Whoever, being a police officer, commits penetrative sexual assault on a child - (a) within the limits of the police station or premises where he is appointed; or (b) in the premises of any station house, whether or not situated in the police station to which he is appointed; or (c) in the course of his official duties; or (d) where he is known as a police officer;

Legal reference: Protection of Children from Sexual Offences (POCSO) Act, 2012,Section 9
Category: Family
Description: (1) Whoever, being a police officer, commits sexual assault on a child - (a) within the limits of the police station or premises where he is appointed; or (b) in the premises of any station house, whether or not situated in the police station to which he is appointed; or (c) in the course of his official duties; or (d) where he is known as a police officer;
